+/* VKD3D fex43: a frame whose spare time came from a busy GPU (the GPU was still on the frame before when the game called
+ * Present(), so the frame had only as much room as the GPU left it) holds its place in the 256-frame memory without
+ * limiting it, like a roomy one (fex41). While the GPU is full such frames allow (nearly) no hold-back, and that is right:
+ * they still count among the last 64 frames (~2 s), and GPU-bound pacing (48 of 64 busy) doesn't use the long memory.
+ * But up to fex42 they also went into the long memory, so after a heavy fight, when the GPU had room again, they kept the
+ * hold-back at 0-3 ms for up to 8.5 s while every new frame had ~15 ms of room. In the FEX build 163 multiplayer log
+ * (GPU 90% busy or more in 241 of 773 s of play) that was 70 s at 66 ms from frame start to screen (median) against ~47 ms:
+ * at t=775-782 the last 64 frames alone allowed 50 ms and the memory, holding the busy frames of t=773-774, 0.6 ms; at
+ * t=455-459, right after GPU-bound pacing, 0 ms. In build 162 (lighter scenes) it was 6 s. Frames late or nearly late with
+ * the hold-back on keep their own rules (fex40), so a busy frame after another such one still goes in.
+ * VKD3D_FEX_START_BUSY_SKIP (0 = off, as fex42). */
